@lang en
IMPORT `bmcar-section-2`

-- THE HOSTILE READING, demonstrated. Each block is a finding in NOTES.md §4 (X-numbers):
-- a defect in the instrument as written, not an ambiguity resolved. Every assertion here
-- states what the TEXT gives on the scenario, worked by hand from the clause cited; that
-- the answer is surprising is the point. A failure here would mean the encoding does not
-- say what the text says.

§ `Findings`

§§ `X3 — cover can begin before the date the Schedule states`

-- The Schedule says 1 March 2026; works began on 15 February. "dù ngày quy định trong phụ
-- lục có thể khác" makes the site event govern, so a loss on 20 February is in the period.
-- (source lines 44-45)
#ASSERT `the occurrence on` (YMD 2026 2 20) `falls within the period of insurance of` `the policy where work began before the Schedule date`

§§ `X4 — a part handed over but not yet used stays on cover`

-- Cover on a part ends only when it is handed over AND put into use.
-- (source lines 47-48)
#ASSERT `Section I — the outcome of the claim` `the policy` `proper conduct of the risk` (`a standard claim for` (LIST `a loss to a part handed over but not yet in use`)) EQUALS `payable` 350_000_000
#ASSERT `Section I — the outcome of the claim` `the policy` `proper conduct of the risk` (`a standard claim for` (LIST `a loss to a part in use but not handed over`)) EQUALS `payable` 350_000_000

§§ `X5 — a notice inside the 14 days still defeats the claim if it was not "immediate"`

-- General Condition 5's own sanction allows 14 days; General Condition 1 makes the duty to
-- notify "lập tức" a condition precedent. Notice received on day 2, not immediate:
-- (source line 89)
-- (source lines 102-104)
#ASSERT `General Condition 5 — Bao Minh received notice within 14 days of the occurrence on` (YMD 2026 6 10) (`the Insured's conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026, notice on day 2 not immediate`'s `the notice`)
#ASSERT `Section I — the outcome of the claim` `the policy` `proper conduct of the risk` (`a Section I claim on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `for` (LIST `the standard loss to the works`) `debris` 0 `consequential` 0 `paid before` 0 `other insurance` FALSE `conduct` `the Insured's conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026, notice on day 2 not immediate` `history` `a clean claim history`) EQUALS `nothing is payable, because` `General Condition 1 — a condition precedent to liability is not met`

§§ `X6 — a written notice without a telegram defeats an unrelated claim`

-- A material change notified promptly in writing, with every precaution taken, but not by
-- telegram; then a storm loss that has nothing to do with the change. General Condition 1
-- has no causation or materiality test, so the storm claim fails.
-- (source lines 76-77)
#ASSERT `Section I — the outcome of the claim` `the policy` `conduct of the risk with a change notified in writing only` (`a standard claim for` (LIST `the standard loss to the works`)) EQUALS `nothing is payable, because` `General Condition 1 — a condition precedent to liability is not met`
-- And a notice of the loss in writing alone, without a telephone call or a telegram.
#ASSERT `Section I — the outcome of the claim` `the policy` `proper conduct of the risk` (`a Section I claim on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `for` (LIST `the standard loss to the works`) `debris` 0 `consequential` 0 `paid before` 0 `other insurance` FALSE `conduct` `the Insured's conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026, notice in writing only` `history` `a clean claim history`) EQUALS `nothing is payable, because` `General Condition 1 — a condition precedent to liability is not met`

§§ `X8 — arbitration can be stalled indefinitely`

-- Bao Minh does not appoint its arbitrator within the month. The duty is breached, but the
-- clause states no consequence, and the award stays a condition precedent to any action:
-- the action is barred for want of an award, with no date after which that stops.
-- (source lines 129-131)
-- (source lines 133-134)
#TRACE `General Condition 7 — the duty of` `Bao Minh` `to appoint an arbitrator after a written request sent on` (YMD 2026 7 15) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
#ASSERT `General Condition 7 — an action against Bao Minh is barred for want of an award` (`General Condition 7 — the difference must be referred to arbitration` TRUE TRUE) NOTHING

§§ `X10 — the General Condition 8 time-bar never reaches an outright rejection`

-- A claim rejected outright in 2026 (liability denied, so not arbitrable under General
-- Condition 7), no proceedings by 2031: the text gives no clock that runs from the
-- rejection, so nothing is forfeited.
-- (source lines 138-141)
#ASSERT NOT `General Condition 7 — the difference must be referred to arbitration` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `General Condition 8 — all benefit under the Policy is forfeited` `rejected outright in 2026, no arbitration, no proceedings, as at 2031`

§§ `X14 — exclusion (d) read with "hạng mục" as the Schedule item`

-- The insuring clause distinguishes "hạng mục" (an item in the Schedule) from "bộ phận" (a
-- part of it), and General Condition 2 keeps a term's meaning wherever it appears. Read so,
-- exclusion (d) is limited to "the items directly affected", which for a defect anywhere in
-- the works is the whole of item 1. A defective beam that costs 20 million to replace and
-- brings down 400 million of the works:
-- src:153 | thời hạn bảo hiểm, một hạng mục nào đó có tên trong Phụ lục hay bất kỳ bộ phận nào của hạng
-- src:154 | mục đó bị tổn thất vật chất bất ngờ và không lường trước được do bất kỳ nguyên nhân nào khác với
-- src:181 | d) Những chi phí thay thế, sửa chữa, chỉnh lý khuyết tật của vật liệu hoặc tay nghề tuy
-- src:182 | nhiên loại trừ này chỉ hạn chế trong chính những hạng mục bị ảnh hưởng trực tiếp, còn
-- src:183 | tổn thất của các hạng mục khác xảy ra do một tai nạn là hậu quả khuyết tật của nguyên
-- src:184 | vật liệu và tay nghề thì không bị loại trừ;
@ref Section I exclusion (d), lines 181-184, on the reading in which an item is a Schedule item (finding X14)
GIVEN l IS A `A loss to an item`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Section I exclusion (d), on the Schedule-item reading — the whole loss to the item is excluded` l MEANS
    elem `defective material or workmanship in the item itself` (l's `the causes`)

-- The reading taken (component): 400 - 20 = 380 million for the item, 330 million after
-- the deductible. The Schedule-item reading: the whole item 1 loss is excluded.
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the loss to the item` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a collapse of the works from one defective beam` EQUALS 380_000_000
#ASSERT `Section I exclusion (d), on the Schedule-item reading — the whole loss to the item is excluded` `a collapse of the works from one defective beam`

§§ `X15 — insured at the new price, paid at the depreciated value`

-- Article I requires plant to be insured at its replacement value new (here 2 billion);
-- Article 2(b) pays a total loss at its actual value before the loss (1.2 billion). The
-- plant is destroyed and replaced new for 2 billion: the Insured recovers 1.2 billion on a
-- premium charged on 2 billion.
-- (source lines 210-211)
-- (source lines 231-232)
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the loss to the item` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a total loss of plant, replaced new` EQUALS 1_200_000_000
-- Insuring it at the 1.2 billion it would be paid instead triggers the average:
-- 1.2 / 2.0 of 1.2 billion = 720 million.
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the loss to the item` `the policy with plant insured at its actual value` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a total loss of plant insured at its actual value` EQUALS 720_000_000

§§ `X16 — the average bites a small early loss`

-- Works insured for 10 billion; the value at completion turns out to be 12.5 billion. Only
-- 1 billion of work exists when 400 million of it is damaged: the sum insured is ten times
-- the value at risk, yet the loss is cut by 10/12.5 to 320 million.
-- (source lines 206-208)
-- (source lines 217-220)
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the loss to the item` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `an early loss to works insured below the completion value` EQUALS 320_000_000

§§ `X17 — nothing is paid until the Insured has paid for the repair or replacement`

-- Plant destroyed, not yet replaced: nothing actually incurred, so nothing payable; and Bao
-- Minh is not yet bound to pay anyway.
-- (source line 234)
-- (source lines 238-240)
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the loss to the item` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a total loss of plant, not yet replaced` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Article 2 — Bao Minh is not yet bound to pay for the loss to the item` `a total loss of plant, not yet replaced`
-- A repair not yet paid for: the same.
#ASSERT `Section I — the indemnity for the loss to the item` `the policy` (YMD 2026 6 10) `a repair not yet paid for` EQUALS 0

§§ `X19 — Bao Minh may buy its way out of a third-party claim`

-- The claim could, in Bao Minh's view, be settled for 2.5 billion; the limit leaves 4
-- billion. Bao Minh pays 2.5 billion and is discharged; if the claimant does not settle
-- and recovers more, or the defence costs more, that is the Insured's.
-- (source lines 321-325)
#ASSERT `Section II Condition 2 — the payment that discharges Bao Minh of the occurrence` 5_000_000_000 1_000_000_000 (JUST 2_500_000_000) EQUALS 2_500_000_000
#ASSERT `Section II Condition 2 — Bao Minh's further liability for the occurrence after it pays` 2_500_000_000 EQUALS 0

§§ `X24 — a work stoppage anywhere in the chain excludes a storm loss`

-- "trực tiếp hay gián tiếp": the site was idle during a strike-free suspension when a storm
-- struck; the stoppage is among the causes, so General Exclusion (d) takes the loss out.
-- (source lines 19-20)
-- (source line 34)
#ASSERT `Section I — the outcome of the claim` `the policy` `proper conduct of the risk` (`a standard claim for` (LIST `a loss caused during a cessation of work`)) EQUALS `nothing is payable, because` `no loss claimed is within the cover`
